    "body": "**Physical iPhone Safari acceptance follow-up: still FAIL on HEAD `49847aa93a57f4ae262110586da9f43cb9590552` (owner screenshots dated Oct 31).** No merge approval. User's native screenshots (4 images, two with red annotations) are being handed to the existing Codex PR #431 workstream as attachments, not hosted in this GitHub comment.\n\n**Exactly four observed items:**\n1. Mobile DM tab with count `0` shows an empty, huge lower region with no clear empty state or accessible conversation; do not claim a transcript should exist when no thread exists. Give helpful empty state and verify real conversations populate when DM exists.\n2. **Top profile/header** (nickname, tone, reputation, balance, stats, Menu) consumes a disproportionate fraction of the viewport, including while editing with native keyboard. Implement a compact, user-friendly mobile/keyboard mode (ideally single condensed row, preserved menu and recoverable stats) that prioritizes actual chat/DM area. This is **not** the `Личка / Баттлы / События` tabstrip: user confirms tab navigation already PASS.\n3. With several DM threads, `#dmLog` visible **message history** area remains only ~2 lines tall between large name chips and actions. DM conversation log is the primary content, should gain usable vertical room and scroll independently, with composer/Send accessible; reduce excess vertical space consumed by DM header/thread chips/action area as warranted. Owner's red oval in screenshot 3 identifies cramped **history**, not just text-input width.\n4. A long pale **horizontal overlay** crosses DM content/actions **only in the Report test scenario** (red oval in screenshot 4); user explicitly confirms it **does not occur in ordinary DM test**. Reproduce both in the isolated UI lab and distinguish PR UI bug vs. test-lab injection or scenario artifact before modifying source. Identify actual element via `elementFromPoint`, computed style, bounding rect and parent chain. Do not hide legitimate resize handles or swipe controls as a blind CSS patch.\n\n**Everything else tested by owner PASS**, including mobile `Личка / Баттлы / События` navigation. Previous Chromium 176/176 and standalone reviewer PASS do not override real iPhone screenshots; add faithful regression cases and run actual browser, Python/Node, mirror parity, CI, independent exact-HEAD review. User must rerun real physical Safari after publishing new HEAD and updating isolated previews.\n\n**Scope:** continue the SAME existing PR #431 and Codex thread. Allowed per ownership approval: `ui-core.js`, `style-base.css`, `ui-dm.js` in exact Web/docs mirrors, plus current regression tests. Check current repo rules/locks before changes, protect all other PRs. No unapproved extra scope; no main, merge, force push, Chat03, Cloudflare deployment, or PR #453 changes. No Safari PASS until owner verifies.",
