    "body": "## Summary\n\n- On the active “Личка” tab, the general chat yields space to the DM panel and restores its preferred height when switching tabs.\n- Short keyboard viewports keep the focused field, DM composer and report suggestions usable. The report list stays attached to its input and scrolls within the visible area.\n- The regression runner checks natural scroll ranges. A separate Playwright test sends trusted wheel input to the DM panel, DM log and report list, then selects the last report suggestion.\n\n## Scope\n\nEight paths differ from the PR base:\n\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-core.js`\n- `docs/ui/ui-core.js`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/style-base.css`\n- `docs/style-base.css`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-dm.js`\n- `docs/ui/ui-dm.js`\n- `tools/test_mobile_shell_regressions.html`\n- `tools/test_mobile_shell_user_scroll.mjs`\n\nAll three Web/docs pairs are byte-identical.\n\n## Verification on exact HEAD `49847aa93a57f4ae262110586da9f43cb9590552`\n\n- Headless Chromium full runner: **176/176 PASS** across 320×568, 360×640, 390×844, 430×932, 768×1024, 1280×720 and 1440×900.\n- **10 fixture-only SKIP**, explicitly excluded from PASS: unavailable battle action entry and saved panel-scroll restoration in five mobile/tablet fixtures.\n- At 320×568, trusted wheel checks passed for revealing the DM log, scrolling to older messages, keeping report suggestions positioned during panel scrolling, reaching the final suggestion and selecting it while retaining input focus.\n- `python3 tools/test_mobile_first_interface_contract.py`: **14/14 PASS**.\n- Node syntax checks, `git diff --check`, and all three mirror comparisons: PASS.\n- GitHub Actions [ai-forensics-evidence #41076444466](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/41076444466): SUCCESS.\n- Independent exact-head review: **PASS**. Mutation checks confirmed that disabling report-list scrolling, DM-log interaction or report-panel repositioning makes the browser test fail.\n\nPhysical iPhone Safari and its native keyboard still require owner verification. This PR remains Draft; these checks do not constitute device acceptance or merge approval.",
